1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:01:22,696 --> 00:01:24,840
When the system crashes, don't just make random guesses.

9
00:01:24,952 --> 00:01:26,280
Check each log one by one.

10
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:28,200
That way, we'll know exactly what's causing the problem.

11
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,121
- Got it?
- Got it.

12
00:01:35,854 --> 00:01:37,760
Munin, where are you now? Or have you just landed?

13
00:01:39,523 --> 00:01:40,524
What?

14
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:42,760
Calm down, okay? I'll come to you right away.

15
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:46,361
[Khao Yai, Saraburi]

16
00:02:11,366 --> 00:02:12,367
Ta!

17
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:13,901
Ta!

18
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:26,800
Where are you, Ta?

19
00:02:29,651 --> 00:02:30,652
Ta!

20
00:02:34,286 --> 00:02:35,287
Ta!

21
00:02:35,774 --> 00:02:36,775
Ta!

22
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:44,591
Ta!

23
00:02:45,056 --> 00:02:46,057
Ta!

24
00:03:03,024 --> 00:03:04,025
Ta!

25
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:05,791
Ta!

26
00:03:06,987 --> 00:03:07,988
Ta!

27
00:03:08,654 --> 00:03:09,655
Ta!

28
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,113
Ta!

29
00:03:17,774 --> 00:03:19,640
Ta! Ta!

30
00:03:19,736 --> 00:03:21,760
Ta! Ta!

31
00:03:21,966 --> 00:03:22,967
Ta!

32
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,441
Ta!

33
00:03:28,544 --> 00:03:29,545
Ta!

34
00:03:30,075 --> 00:03:31,800
Ta!

35
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:33,791
Ta!

36
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,121
Ta!

37
00:03:42,643 --> 00:03:43,644
Ta!

38
00:05:30,659 --> 00:05:31,660
Munin!

39
00:05:32,435 --> 00:05:33,720
What happened to your sister?

40
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,721
I don't know.

41
00:05:37,891 --> 00:05:38,892
When I got here,

42
00:05:39,918 --> 00:05:41,320
there was blood all over the house.

43
00:05:43,363 --> 00:05:44,800
I followed the trail of blood

44
00:05:45,672 --> 00:05:48,320
and found Ta's lifeless body in the water, all pale.

45
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,521
She must've been dead for hours.

46
00:05:53,238 --> 00:05:54,880
Have you called the police yet?

47
00:05:56,624 --> 00:05:57,625
No.

48
00:05:59,216 --> 00:06:00,760
Ta didn't want anyone to know about this.

49
00:06:02,782 --> 00:06:04,787
She sent me this message before she died.

50
00:06:12,454 --> 00:06:15,000
I'm glad we were born as sisters.

51
00:06:16,102 --> 00:06:17,103
I'm sorry

52
00:06:17,467 --> 00:06:20,000
I couldn't make our dream come true.

53
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,040
In our next life,

54
00:06:22,912 --> 00:06:24,840
I promise I'll make it happen.

55
00:06:25,522 --> 00:06:27,080
I hope you'll be happy.

56
00:06:27,851 --> 00:06:29,640
Live your life for both of us.

57
00:06:30,374 --> 00:06:31,920
And don't tell anyone about this.

58
00:06:32,824 --> 00:06:34,563
Don't try to find out the truth.

59
00:06:35,054 --> 00:06:36,700
It's all my fault.

60
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:40,720
Please let me go quietly and peacefully.

61
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:42,391
Goodbye.

62
00:06:43,499 --> 00:06:44,500
What does this mean, Munin?

63
00:06:45,718 --> 00:06:47,080
What happened to your sister?

64
00:06:47,979 --> 00:06:49,200
I'm wondering the same thing.

65
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,100
We were talking just fine before I boarded my flight yesterday.

66
00:06:52,118 --> 00:06:53,800
How could this have happened?

67
00:06:59,803 --> 00:07:00,804
Munin.

68
00:07:02,987 --> 00:07:04,250
Calm down, okay?

69
00:07:06,128 --> 00:07:08,329
I think we should do what needs to be done first.

70
00:07:08,955 --> 00:07:10,680
Your sister died under suspicious circumstances.

71
00:07:10,928 --> 00:07:12,440
We have to report this to the police.

72
00:07:13,286 --> 00:07:15,600
And let the forensic experts determine the cause of her death.

73
00:07:16,779 --> 00:07:17,780
No.

74
00:07:18,502 --> 00:07:20,160
Ta didn't want me to tell anyone about this.

75
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,600
I think there's something more to this.

76
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,160
The more Ta tries to stop me from finding out the truth,

77
00:07:25,851 --> 00:07:26,980
the more I want to know.

78
00:07:28,464 --> 00:07:29,640
I'll investigate it myself.

79
00:07:31,104 --> 00:07:32,105
Investigate?

80
00:07:33,182 --> 00:07:34,360
How are you going to do that?

81
00:07:34,424 --> 00:07:36,600
You're a programmer, not a detective!

82
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,040
When a server crashes,

83
00:07:40,558 --> 00:07:41,640
you check the logs

84
00:07:41,966 --> 00:07:43,160
and go through them one by one

85
00:07:43,574 --> 00:07:44,960
to find out where something went wrong.

86
00:07:45,094 --> 00:07:47,240
Then you fix each issue and rule out what's not relevant.

87
00:07:47,366 --> 00:07:49,900
Eventually, you'll find the root cause, right?

88
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,120
But what are you going to do with her body?

89
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,281
Ta.

90
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,281
Come stay at my place for now.

91
00:08:27,995 --> 00:08:29,680
We're already halfway to making our dream come true.

92
00:08:30,203 --> 00:08:31,404
I'm waiting for the other half.

93
00:08:32,368 --> 00:08:33,400
It won't be long now.

94
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,712
I've almost saved up enough money.

95
00:08:36,287 --> 00:08:37,720
Once I've got enough,

96
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:39,640
we'll start building right away.

97
00:08:40,502 --> 00:08:42,240
Once I've wrapped up my work in America,

98
00:08:42,507 --> 00:08:44,008
I'll hurry back and move into our house.

99
00:10:08,579 --> 00:10:09,580
Munin.

100
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,401
Are you sure this is what you really want?

101
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:18,720
Wouldn't it be better to take Ta's body to a temple?

102
00:10:21,736 --> 00:10:24,180
I want her to stay in this house for as long as possible

103
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,520
until I find out the truth

104
00:10:28,347 --> 00:10:29,800
about what happened to her.

105
00:10:31,915 --> 00:10:33,760
But we've already searched the whole house.

106
00:10:34,432 --> 00:10:36,840
There were no signs of forced entry or a struggle.

107
00:10:37,464 --> 00:10:39,180
There weren't any wounds on her body either.

108
00:10:39,890 --> 00:10:41,891
It doesn't look like murder at all.

109
00:10:42,766 --> 00:10:44,400
Is it possible that your sister might have...

110
00:10:47,536 --> 00:10:48,537
I'm sorry,

111
00:10:50,155 --> 00:10:51,520
but maybe she really did take her own life.

112
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:54,831
Then take a look at this.

113
00:11:07,939 --> 00:11:09,920
Ta invited me to have dinner with her tonight.

114
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:12,520
She stocked the fridge with food.

115
00:11:13,608 --> 00:11:15,609
She didn't seem like someone planning to take her own life.

116
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:18,830
Maybe something suddenly happened that upset her,

117
00:11:18,888 --> 00:11:20,880
and she made an impulsive decision.

118
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,100
But we can't rule out murder either.

119
00:11:24,161 --> 00:11:26,400
Even though there were no signs of a struggle or injuries,

120
00:11:27,334 --> 00:11:29,080
Ta could have been poisoned.

121
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,520
All that blood around the house

122
00:11:32,064 --> 00:11:33,760
might have been blood she vomited up.

123
00:11:34,496 --> 00:11:36,840
That's why we need an autopsy, Munin.

124
00:11:37,686 --> 00:11:40,280
I told you, Ta didn't want anyone to know about this.

125
00:11:54,976 --> 00:11:55,977
Munin.

126
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:58,440
I'm not your enemy, you know.

127
00:11:59,326 --> 00:12:00,600
I'm your friend.

128
00:12:01,795 --> 00:12:02,796
I'm here to help.

129
00:12:17,150 --> 00:12:18,151
I'm sorry.

130
00:12:20,598 --> 00:12:21,800
But please, I'm begging you.

131
00:12:22,691 --> 00:12:24,100
Don't let anyone find out about this.

132
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:26,840
I'll investigate everything myself.

133
00:12:28,936 --> 00:12:29,937
Fine.

134
00:12:30,835 --> 00:12:32,420
If that's what you want, so be it.

135
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,440
Then I'll help you investigate.

136
00:13:39,115 --> 00:13:40,116
Munin.

137
00:13:43,931 --> 00:13:44,932
Are you really going to do this?

138
00:13:47,083 --> 00:13:48,120
What's the big deal?

139
00:13:49,376 --> 00:13:50,377
Or are you scared?

140
00:13:56,603 --> 00:13:57,720
I'm not scared.

141
00:14:01,158 --> 00:14:02,560
It just feels weird.

142
00:14:44,827 --> 00:14:46,160
Go ahead and open it.

143
00:14:46,390 --> 00:14:49,440
If you want to know what happened to your sister, you'll have to open it anyway.

144
00:15:05,606 --> 00:15:08,760
Start by checking her chats. See who Ta last talked to.

145
00:15:09,152 --> 00:15:11,440
Then check her call history and photo album.

146
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:13,240
And all her social media apps, too.

147
00:15:13,696 --> 00:15:15,267
I'm sure we'll find some clues.

148
00:15:41,878 --> 00:15:43,563
How's it going? Found anything?

149
00:15:44,256 --> 00:15:46,057
I found a suspicious guy.

150
00:15:49,099 --> 00:15:51,440
Who? Your sister's boyfriend?

151
00:15:51,968 --> 00:15:52,969
I don't think so.

152
00:15:53,264 --> 00:15:55,250
There aren't any pictures of him in Ta's album.

153
00:15:55,408 --> 00:15:56,840
But on his Facebook page,

154
00:15:56,918 --> 00:15:58,720
there are tons of selfies with Ta.

155
00:15:58,811 --> 00:16:00,560
And Ta doesn't look happy in any of them.

156
00:16:02,683 --> 00:16:04,720
Maybe he was pursuing her?

157
00:16:05,216 --> 00:16:07,440
And when she rejected him, he hurt her.

158
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:09,385
That's possible.

159
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,326
But Ta told me she had a boyfriend.

160
00:16:12,779 --> 00:16:14,360
She just hadn't introduced him to me yet.

161
00:16:14,587 --> 00:16:15,800
She said she wanted to be sure about him first.

162
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,640
Anything else interesting on her phone?

163
00:16:23,136 --> 00:16:24,920
Her chats are all about work.

164
00:16:25,382 --> 00:16:28,280
Apart from her coworkers, she doesn't seem to have any other friends.

165
00:16:28,587 --> 00:16:30,360
She never goes out or has any hobbies.

166
00:16:31,179 --> 00:16:33,000
Oh, I found something in her calendar.

167
00:16:33,414 --> 00:16:35,699
She had a doctor's appointment on the 12th.

168
00:16:35,864 --> 00:16:37,280
But I have no idea what kind of doctor.

169
00:16:39,891 --> 00:16:41,539
Try checking her contacts.

170
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
See if she saved any doctors' numbers.

171
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:47,250
There's only one doctor in here.

172
00:16:48,731 --> 00:16:49,732
Then call!

173
00:16:56,950 --> 00:16:57,951
Hello.

174
00:16:58,438 --> 00:17:00,080
How can I help you, Mutta?

175
00:17:01,323 --> 00:17:03,686
Um, Doctor.

176
00:17:03,872 --> 00:17:05,760
Our appointment is on the 12th, right?

177
00:17:06,268 --> 00:17:08,920
Just a moment. Let me check my schedule.

178
00:17:10,608 --> 00:17:13,560
Yes, it's on the 12th at 1 p.m.

179
00:17:14,251 --> 00:17:17,240
Could we move it up to tomorrow?

180
00:17:33,896 --> 00:17:35,440
You told me not to tell anyone about this.

181
00:17:36,742 --> 00:17:37,960
I'm okay with that.

182
00:17:40,155 --> 00:17:42,080
But asking me not to look for the truth

183
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:44,880
is something I just can't do.

184
00:17:46,896 --> 00:17:48,280
You are dead, for God's sake!

185
00:17:50,343 --> 00:17:52,044
But if you don't want me to go through all this trouble,

186
00:17:53,206 --> 00:17:55,120
then help me uncover the truth soon.

187
00:18:44,070 --> 00:18:47,280
Did you get a haircut, Ta? You look so refreshed!

188
00:18:48,344 --> 00:18:49,741
Oh, yes.

189
00:18:50,392 --> 00:18:53,080
I've been feeling a little bored, so I wanted to try something new.

190
00:18:54,184 --> 00:18:55,185
I'm glad

191
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:58,723
you're taking steps to overcome your boredom by making a change.

192
00:18:59,934 --> 00:19:01,120
Let me ask you something.

193
00:19:01,667 --> 00:19:04,000
Is there something in particular that's making you feel bored?

194
00:19:04,030 --> 00:19:05,880
Or are you just bored with everything?

195
00:19:08,011 --> 00:19:09,160
Let's put that aside for now.

196
00:19:09,984 --> 00:19:13,790
There's something I'd like to ask you today, Doctor.

197
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:17,320
Sorry, I forgot you rescheduled because you had something urgent to discuss.

198
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:18,921
What is it?

199
00:19:21,731 --> 00:19:24,216
By the way, how many times have we met?

200
00:19:25,730 --> 00:19:27,166
This is our second session.

201
00:19:30,139 --> 00:19:31,640
What did we talk about during our first session?

202
00:19:33,275 --> 00:19:35,720
Are you asking because you can't remember, Mutta?

203
00:19:37,019 --> 00:19:39,520
I've been a little forgetful lately.

204
00:19:39,832 --> 00:19:41,795
So I was hoping you could give me a quick recap

205
00:19:41,950 --> 00:19:43,451
of what we've already discussed.

206
00:19:43,896 --> 00:19:46,400
That way, we won't repeat ourselves.

207
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:49,520
Well, last time,

208
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:52,134
you talked about things at the office.

209
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:54,000
Problems with various coworkers.

210
00:19:55,707 --> 00:19:57,400
Was there anyone in particular I had a problem with?

211
00:19:58,027 --> 00:20:00,400
I take all the problems you've had

212
00:20:00,428 --> 00:20:02,300
with your coworkers equally seriously.

213
00:20:02,646 --> 00:20:04,920
I can't say any one issue is more important than another.

214
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,001
What about my love life?

215
00:20:08,464 --> 00:20:09,560
Did I tell you anything about that?

216
00:20:11,072 --> 00:20:12,240
No, you didn't.

217
00:20:13,785 --> 00:20:15,702
We spent the entire last session talking about work.

218
00:20:15,730 --> 00:20:17,400
And that alone took an hour and a half.

219
00:20:19,155 --> 00:20:21,000
You even told me yourself

220
00:20:21,056 --> 00:20:24,080
that you'd tell me about a major problem in your life this time.

221
00:20:24,670 --> 00:20:26,720
I've been waiting to hear what it is.

222
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:29,601
A major problem?

223
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:32,760
Did I give you any hints about what it was?

224
00:20:34,387 --> 00:20:35,960
I already asked you about it.

225
00:20:36,424 --> 00:20:39,760
But you said you'd tell me everything when you came back.

226
00:20:42,451 --> 00:20:43,600
Are you ready to talk about it now?

227
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:50,560
So,

228
00:20:52,176 --> 00:20:54,680
am I really talking to Mutta right now?

229
00:21:07,443 --> 00:21:09,680
Munin, I'm asking you one more time.

230
00:21:09,848 --> 00:21:11,240
Are you sure you want to do this?

231
00:21:12,195 --> 00:21:13,800
If we keep investigating as outsiders,

232
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:16,160
we'll never know the details of Ta's life.

233
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:19,440
The only way to find out what happened to Ta

234
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:21,600
is for me to become her.

235
00:21:22,179 --> 00:21:23,600
To live her life.

236
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:32,880
But will you be able to pull it off?

237
00:21:33,224 --> 00:21:34,880
Are you sure no one will catch on?

238
00:21:36,051 --> 00:21:38,120
No disguise is ever perfect.

239
00:21:39,035 --> 00:21:40,480
It's just like writing code.

240
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,920
There are bound to be bugs.

241
00:21:43,824 --> 00:21:47,200
My job is to make sure no one finds those bugs,

242
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,280
or at least not until it's too late.

243
00:22:06,862 --> 00:22:08,440
I've sent you information on the suspects

244
00:22:08,463 --> 00:22:10,422
at the ministry who may be connected to your sister.

245
00:22:11,392 --> 00:22:12,720
You need to be careful, Munin.

246
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,920
I know it's risky.

247
00:22:16,342 --> 00:22:19,320
But it's the only way I'll find out

248
00:22:20,352 --> 00:22:21,480
who did this to my sister.

249
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,101
[VeeKit Jetsadapiban]

250
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:12,200
The two of us look so much alike

251
00:23:13,491 --> 00:23:15,160
that people have had trouble telling us apart since we were kids.

252
00:23:18,835 --> 00:23:20,200
We always hated it

253
00:23:20,910 --> 00:23:22,360
when adults mixed us up.

254
00:23:26,496 --> 00:23:27,920
Sometimes, when you misbehaved,

255
00:23:29,254 --> 00:23:30,720
I was the one who got punished.

256
00:23:33,547 --> 00:23:35,558
Other times, I'd get two treats

257
00:23:36,347 --> 00:23:37,348
while you got none.

258
00:23:41,984 --> 00:23:43,440
We both agreed

259
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:47,800
that there was no point in God creating

260
00:23:49,096 --> 00:23:50,720
two people who looked exactly alike.

261
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:58,100
But today, I'm finally going to put it to good use.

262
00:24:52,192 --> 00:24:53,193
Ta.

263
00:24:54,891 --> 00:24:55,960
I'm going to pretend to be you

264
00:24:58,128 --> 00:24:59,440
to uncover the truth

265
00:25:01,312 --> 00:25:02,760
about what caused your death.

266
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:06,732
Ta!

267
00:26:08,220 --> 00:26:09,960
I missed you so much, my sis!

268
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:15,960
Ta, where have you been?

269
00:26:16,072 --> 00:26:18,840
Do you know how worried we've been about you?

270
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:21,880
I went on a meditation retreat.

271
00:26:22,256 --> 00:26:25,120
I'm feeling better now and ready to get back to work.

272
00:26:25,547 --> 00:26:27,088
That's good to hear, Ta.

273
00:26:27,552 --> 00:26:29,440
Because ever since you've been gone,

274
00:26:29,704 --> 00:26:32,760
Meow and Aunt Phorn have been taking everything out on me.

275
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:35,920
You came back just in time, Ta.

276
00:26:36,201 --> 00:26:38,800
Otherwise, I would've quit!

277
00:26:39,646 --> 00:26:42,400
You make it sound like our office is such a terrible place.

278
00:26:42,915 --> 00:26:44,816
Oh, come on! As if you haven't been through it yourself.

279
00:26:44,840 --> 00:26:47,475
You disappeared on a meditation retreat for two whole weeks.

280
00:26:47,624 --> 00:26:51,520
Wasn't it partly because those nasty women were bullying you?

281
00:26:53,054 --> 00:26:54,055
That's true.

282
00:26:54,798 --> 00:26:56,050
I've been stressed out about a lot of things.

283
00:26:56,734 --> 00:26:57,735
Just a moment.

284
00:27:07,256 --> 00:27:08,960
I brought some snacks for you, too.

285
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:11,260
- Thank you so much, Ta.
- Thank you, Ta.

286
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:12,920
- They look delicious!
- Curry puffs!

287
00:27:14,232 --> 00:27:15,280
Oh, Ta!

288
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:23,121
Let's go.

289
00:27:50,486 --> 00:27:53,487
Ta, aren't you going to get coffee today?

290
00:27:54,848 --> 00:27:55,849
Oh.

291
00:27:56,150 --> 00:27:57,400
I totally forgot. Let's go!

292
00:27:57,883 --> 00:28:01,160
How could you forget our daily routine?

293
00:28:18,702 --> 00:28:20,200
- The usual, please.
- Sure.

294
00:28:20,216 --> 00:28:21,617
- The usual for me, too.
- Sure.

295
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:23,454
I'll have my usual, too.

296
00:28:23,758 --> 00:28:24,759
Sure.

297
00:28:25,134 --> 00:28:27,760
Oh, Ta! I haven't seen you in days.

298
00:28:27,854 --> 00:28:29,080
Have you put on a little weight?

299
00:28:30,366 --> 00:28:31,367
Maybe a little.

300
00:28:33,288 --> 00:28:35,280
Veekit, your order's ready!

301
00:28:37,315 --> 00:28:38,920
I'll take it to him.

302
00:28:39,470 --> 00:28:40,471
I'll take it myself.

303
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:07,761
Ta?

304
00:29:13,494 --> 00:29:14,495
Where have you been?

305
00:29:16,224 --> 00:29:17,760
Why? Did you miss me?

306
00:29:23,491 --> 00:29:25,560
You mean you were worried about me?

307
00:29:27,614 --> 00:29:28,640
Of course I was.

308
00:29:28,894 --> 00:29:30,800
You disappeared without telling anyone, and no one could reach you.

309
00:29:33,144 --> 00:29:36,120
I went on a meditation retreat. We had to observe silence

310
00:29:36,211 --> 00:29:37,212
and turn off our phones.

311
00:29:42,104 --> 00:29:43,105
So what happened?

312
00:29:43,928 --> 00:29:45,520
Why did you need a two-week meditation retreat?

313
00:29:48,035 --> 00:29:49,640
You should be asking yourself that.

314
00:29:51,438 --> 00:29:52,680
Did you do something to hurt me?

315
00:29:54,984 --> 00:29:55,985
Who hurt whom?

316
00:29:56,483 --> 00:29:57,720
You're the one who hurt me.

317
00:30:00,083 --> 00:30:01,084
Really?

318
00:30:01,475 --> 00:30:02,840
I was the one who hurt you?

319
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:05,200
Your coffee's ready, Ta.

320
00:30:08,051 --> 00:30:09,052
Here you go.

321
00:30:10,035 --> 00:30:11,480
Come on, Ta. Let's hurry upstairs.

322
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:13,720
We need to finish discussing that insurance policy.

323
00:30:14,091 --> 00:30:15,092
Let's go.

324
00:30:29,102 --> 00:30:31,320
This accident insurance policy is fantastic!

325
00:30:31,411 --> 00:30:34,763
Especially after you went tumbling down these stairs.

326
00:30:34,966 --> 00:30:37,720
Even though it wasn't an accident, if you buy insurance from me,

327
00:30:37,835 --> 00:30:41,360
I can make it look like one.

328
00:30:41,718 --> 00:30:42,719
Fell down the stairs?

329
00:30:44,366 --> 00:30:46,760
You're still traumatized by what happened that day, aren't you?

330
00:30:47,203 --> 00:30:48,360
I understand.

331
00:30:48,856 --> 00:30:51,040
Anyone who went through what you did

332
00:30:51,086 --> 00:30:52,650
would be traumatized.

333
00:30:54,331 --> 00:30:56,720
Who... pushed me down the stairs again?

334
00:30:58,870 --> 00:31:01,080
Are you trying to trick me into saying the forbidden story?

335
00:31:01,115 --> 00:31:02,920
No way! I'm not saying it.

336
00:31:04,763 --> 00:31:05,764
The forbidden story?

337
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:09,331
What was it again? Could you remind me?

338
00:31:09,387 --> 00:31:10,720
There you go again!

339
00:31:10,899 --> 00:31:12,400
Let's get back to talking about insurance.

340
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:14,560
If you'd broken your neck and died falling down those stairs,

341
00:31:14,570 --> 00:31:16,300
the insurance would've paid out a million baht.

342
00:31:16,350 --> 00:31:19,500
But if you'd only fractured your elbow, it would've covered your treatment
until you recovered.

343
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:20,803
It's such a great policy.

344
00:31:20,910 --> 00:31:21,911
Wait a minute, Ta.

345
00:31:23,150 --> 00:31:24,960
Where did the scar on your elbow go?

346
00:31:25,422 --> 00:31:27,480
The one from when you fell down the stairs.

347
00:31:29,118 --> 00:31:31,840
I used some cream and got laser treatments, so it healed quickly.

348
00:31:32,278 --> 00:31:35,279
Amazing! Your skin's so smooth, it's like you never had a scar.

349
00:31:35,646 --> 00:31:38,240
I really think you should get this policy.

350
00:31:38,334 --> 00:31:40,120
You never know when you might fall down the stairs again.

351
00:31:40,135 --> 00:31:41,240
Trust me, it's worth it.

352
00:31:43,700 --> 00:31:47,440
Please buy a policy from me. I haven't sold a single one this month.

353
00:31:56,078 --> 00:31:59,079
- Ms. Nopnapha is here! Hello, Nopnapha!
- Hello, ma'am.

354
00:31:59,464 --> 00:32:04,160
Ma'am, could you tell us about the Ministry's latest policies?

355
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:08,171
Since we raised the tax rate to 8% three years ago,

356
00:32:08,779 --> 00:32:13,320
GDP has grown by 3%, 4%, and 4.5%, respectively.

357
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:15,480
This clearly demonstrates

358
00:32:15,550 --> 00:32:17,051
that we've been able to manage

359
00:32:17,126 --> 00:32:19,680
taxpayers' money efficiently.

360
00:32:20,078 --> 00:32:23,100
And I've already discussed next year's budget with
the Ministry of Social Development and Human Security.

361
00:32:23,120 --> 00:32:26,121
We'll be increasing welfare funding for adults,

362
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:29,040
the elderly, as well as mothers and children.

363
00:32:29,294 --> 00:32:31,280
And regarding the development plan to be announced next year,

364
00:32:31,295 --> 00:32:32,960
what direction are you planning to take?

365
00:32:33,091 --> 00:32:34,520
You'll have to ask the Prime Minister about that.

366
00:32:34,592 --> 00:32:37,400
I'm not even on the committee.

367
00:32:37,491 --> 00:32:39,400
I'd rather focus on doing my own job as best I can.

368
00:32:39,539 --> 00:32:42,960
What do you think about the growing public sentiment

369
00:32:43,075 --> 00:32:47,120
that you should replace the current Prime Minister?

370
00:32:48,163 --> 00:32:49,560
I'd rather you didn't say that.

371
00:32:49,600 --> 00:32:51,601
Prime Minister Narong is still in office.

372
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:54,881
We're all cabinet members working together as a team.

373
00:32:55,288 --> 00:32:57,100
If there's nothing else, please excuse me.

374
00:32:57,117 --> 00:32:58,120
Just one more question, ma'am.

375
00:32:58,536 --> 00:33:01,360
Have you done something different lately?

376
00:33:01,432 --> 00:33:05,480
You seem much more radiant than you did a few months ago.

377
00:33:05,536 --> 00:33:07,920
What's your secret to looking so good?

378
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:11,080
Yes, you look much more radiant, ma'am.

379
00:33:11,526 --> 00:33:15,200
I simply got rid of something that had been bothering me.

380
00:33:17,043 --> 00:33:20,760
Every problem must be dealt with directly and decisively.

381
00:33:20,926 --> 00:33:22,170
Only then can we have peace of mind.

382
00:33:24,500 --> 00:33:25,501
Thank you.

383
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:27,521
- Thank you, ma'am.
- Thank you very much, ma'am.

384
00:33:29,835 --> 00:33:32,000
So, how was I? Did I seem like a good person?

385
00:33:32,747 --> 00:33:33,840
Very much so, ma'am.

386
00:33:37,848 --> 00:33:40,451
Hey! Turn it to the left!

387
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:43,000
That's right!

388
00:33:44,078 --> 00:33:46,480
- I said left!
- Hey!

389
00:33:46,926 --> 00:33:48,560
Your left or my left?

390
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:50,160
Chom's left.

391
00:33:50,899 --> 00:33:52,960
What? My left?

392
00:33:53,342 --> 00:33:55,680
But which way is left and which is right?

393
00:33:57,774 --> 00:34:00,600
You're all so stupid! How did you even get jobs at the ministry?

394
00:34:00,654 --> 00:34:02,440
Get down! I'll do it myself!

395
00:34:03,016 --> 00:34:05,960
- How hard can it be?
- Fine! Let the expert do it herself!

396
00:34:07,288 --> 00:34:11,240
Oh, no need to tidy up anymore! The desk's owner is back!

397
00:34:13,144 --> 00:34:16,160
Oh my goodness, Ta!

398
00:34:16,624 --> 00:34:19,678
Where have you been? Look at all those bags!

399
00:34:20,127 --> 00:34:22,600
Exactly! Where have you been?

400
00:34:22,863 --> 00:34:24,320
If you hadn't come back in another two days,

401
00:34:24,751 --> 00:34:26,752
we would've reported you missing.

402
00:34:27,982 --> 00:34:30,920
Were you sick? Did you go away for treatment?

403
00:34:31,651 --> 00:34:32,707
Or do you have AIDS?

404
00:34:35,747 --> 00:34:37,870
You were gone so long, I thought you were dead.

405
00:34:37,982 --> 00:34:39,280
I guess you don't care about your job anymore.

406
00:34:40,776 --> 00:34:43,640
Ta, I missed you so much.

407
00:34:44,067 --> 00:34:46,250
I thought I'd never see you again.

408
00:34:46,710 --> 00:34:50,360
- I'm about to cry!
- It's okay.

409
00:34:51,771 --> 00:34:53,952
Everyone, I...

410
00:34:55,366 --> 00:34:58,000
I went on a meditation retreat in Saraburi.

411
00:34:58,603 --> 00:35:00,040
I'm sorry I made you all worry.

412
00:35:00,208 --> 00:35:01,440
I brought some gifts for everyone, too.

413
00:35:05,344 --> 00:35:07,440
Um, what kind of snacks are these?

414
00:35:07,862 --> 00:35:08,863
They're curry puffs.

415
00:35:08,907 --> 00:35:09,908
Oh!

416
00:35:10,278 --> 00:35:12,440
Eat one, and you'll be a curry...

417
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:13,501
- Puff!
- Puff!

418
00:35:15,203 --> 00:35:17,560
I love chicken-filled curry puffs!

419
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:19,961
Oh, they smell amazing!

420
00:35:20,278 --> 00:35:21,920
Hey, hey!

421
00:35:22,571 --> 00:35:24,572
Gossiping first thing in the morning, huh?

422
00:35:25,462 --> 00:35:28,800
- Get back to work!
- Yes, sir.

423
00:35:32,608 --> 00:35:35,078
Oh, Ta! You're back?

424
00:35:36,715 --> 00:35:37,716
Yes.

425
00:35:44,139 --> 00:35:45,640
Ta, let me help you.

426
00:35:47,942 --> 00:35:48,943
Your chair.

427
00:35:54,123 --> 00:35:56,320
You took time off without submitting a leave request.

428
00:35:56,651 --> 00:35:57,960
That's a serious disciplinary violation.

429
00:36:01,067 --> 00:36:02,507
According to the rules, I should dismiss you.

430
00:36:03,926 --> 00:36:06,040
But I was only absent for 10 working days.

431
00:36:06,187 --> 00:36:07,320
Don't you have to be absent for 14 days

432
00:36:07,760 --> 00:36:09,040
before you can be dismissed?

433
00:36:14,251 --> 00:36:15,440
But it'll still go on your record.

434
00:36:16,822 --> 00:36:19,000
I wanted to promote you to department head

435
00:36:19,023 --> 00:36:20,224
after I retire.

436
00:36:20,758 --> 00:36:21,960
But now that you've done this...

437
00:36:23,168 --> 00:36:26,200
She should be disqualified from becoming department head, Toey.

438
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,920
Phorn! Sak! Who let you two in?

439
00:36:30,024 --> 00:36:31,843
We just couldn't keep quiet about this any longer!

440
00:36:32,682 --> 00:36:36,851
By seniority, I should be the one to succeed you, Toey.

441
00:36:37,048 --> 00:36:40,040
And Sak should be next in line after me.

442
00:36:40,870 --> 00:36:41,871
Who does this little brat think she is?

443
00:36:42,102 --> 00:36:44,080
How can she just jump ahead of us like that?

444
00:36:45,542 --> 00:36:46,760
When choosing a department head,

445
00:36:47,152 --> 00:36:49,040
age isn't the only thing we consider.

446
00:36:50,019 --> 00:36:51,280
We take several factors into account.

447
00:36:53,165 --> 00:36:54,240
But that Mutta

448
00:36:54,900 --> 00:36:57,760
lacks experience and has a terrible attitude.

449
00:36:58,019 --> 00:36:59,920
And she's completely incompetent!

450
00:37:00,235 --> 00:37:02,280
What are you basing your decision on, Toey?

451
00:37:06,246 --> 00:37:07,800
I see potential in her

452
00:37:09,619 --> 00:37:10,654
that you two fail to see.

453
00:37:23,592 --> 00:37:24,593
Ma'am.

454
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,001
What is it?

455
00:37:29,768 --> 00:37:30,800
So that bitch is back?

456
00:37:31,491 --> 00:37:32,680
What kind of shape is she in?

457
00:37:35,048 --> 00:37:36,500
Keep an eye on her.

458
00:37:37,478 --> 00:37:39,480
That bitch is really hard to get rid of!

459
00:37:59,907 --> 00:38:02,600
Ta, is something wrong?

460
00:38:02,990 --> 00:38:05,160
You've been staring at your computer screen for ages.

461
00:38:07,566 --> 00:38:08,880
I can't log into my computer.

462
00:38:09,144 --> 00:38:11,840
I wonder if someone changed my password as a prank.

463
00:38:13,368 --> 00:38:14,480
Let me take a look.

464
00:38:21,834 --> 00:38:22,835
Huh?

465
00:38:23,144 --> 00:38:26,320
It's still 654321, just like before.

466
00:38:27,683 --> 00:38:28,684
Oh, really?

467
00:38:29,053 --> 00:38:31,400
I must've forgotten to switch the keyboard language earlier.

468
00:38:32,614 --> 00:38:33,615
Okay.

469
00:38:33,856 --> 00:38:35,600
By the way, how do you know my computer password?

470
00:38:38,923 --> 00:38:41,480
I happened to see you enter it once.

471
00:38:41,739 --> 00:38:44,200
And it's really easy to remember.

472
00:38:45,435 --> 00:38:47,496
But I've never secretly accessed your computer.

473
00:38:47,536 --> 00:38:48,810
I swear I've never done that.

474
00:38:56,374 --> 00:38:57,979
Um, Hong.

475
00:39:00,208 --> 00:39:01,920
The day I fell down the stairs outside the building,

476
00:39:03,219 --> 00:39:04,320
you were there too, weren't you?

477
00:39:08,371 --> 00:39:09,700
Of course I was.

478
00:39:10,990 --> 00:39:13,200
I was standing right at the front of the crowd.

479
00:39:15,299 --> 00:39:17,840
Then could you tell me what happened again?

480
00:39:18,627 --> 00:39:20,800
What exactly happened before I fell?

481
00:39:21,451 --> 00:39:24,880
I was feeling dizzy at the time,

482
00:39:25,366 --> 00:39:27,424
and I couldn't see clearly. Everything was a blur.

483
00:39:32,955 --> 00:39:34,200
Actually,

484
00:39:34,635 --> 00:39:37,800
we were told not to talk about it, Ta.

485
00:39:39,494 --> 00:39:41,380
But if you really want to bring it up again,

486
00:39:41,886 --> 00:39:44,840
I can tell you a little.

487
00:39:48,366 --> 00:39:49,440
That day,

488
00:39:49,928 --> 00:39:52,600
there was a huge crowd outside the ministry.

489
00:39:53,443 --> 00:39:55,360
Everyone was looking up at the stairs.

490
00:39:56,526 --> 00:39:58,080
Someone had you in a tight grip.

491
00:39:58,227 --> 00:40:01,960
You were slapped again and again!

492
00:40:02,171 --> 00:40:04,360
Oops! Sorry! Did I hit you?

493
00:40:04,440 --> 00:40:06,520
I didn't mean to, Ta.

494
00:40:06,731 --> 00:40:07,760
- Did that hurt?
- Hey!

495
00:40:07,910 --> 00:40:09,184
Hey! What are you gossiping about?

496
00:40:10,136 --> 00:40:12,080
Don't tell me you're talking about that day.

497
00:40:12,747 --> 00:40:13,920
Do you all have a death wish?

498
00:40:14,478 --> 00:40:17,040
No! I was just helping Ta…

499
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:19,960
by swatting a mosquito.

500
00:40:20,058 --> 00:40:22,240
And I was just about to get back to work.

501
00:40:22,944 --> 00:40:24,145
I've got so much to do.

502
00:40:30,374 --> 00:40:32,760
So no one helped me that day?

503
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:38,240
Who would've dared, Ta?

504
00:40:39,598 --> 00:40:43,640
Only Veekit took you to the hospital.

505
00:40:45,995 --> 00:40:48,360
But you weren't seriously hurt, were you?

506
00:40:48,790 --> 00:40:52,210
You even came back to work for another month afterward.

507
00:40:55,394 --> 00:40:56,800
But I understand, Ta.

508
00:40:57,406 --> 00:41:00,200
Emotional wounds take longer to heal.

509
00:41:00,862 --> 00:41:04,400
That's why you went on a two-week meditation retreat, right, Ta?

510
00:41:06,174 --> 00:41:09,288
Hong! Don't you ever shut up?

511
00:41:09,587 --> 00:41:12,400
Come here and help me lick these stamps.

512
00:41:12,563 --> 00:41:15,000
There are hundreds of envelopes. Let me see your tongue.

513
00:41:16,691 --> 00:41:20,480
Come on! Help me stamp all these letters! There are so many.

514
00:41:21,093 --> 00:41:22,094
Okay.

515
00:41:33,814 --> 00:41:34,815
Stick out your tongue!

516
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:48,601
Oh, you're here.

517
00:41:50,460 --> 00:41:51,600
Why did you buy so much food?

518
00:41:53,038 --> 00:41:54,360
Well, you asked to meet at noon.

519
00:41:55,139 --> 00:41:56,200
Aren't you going to have lunch?

520
00:41:59,856 --> 00:42:01,360
How did you know what I wanted to eat?

521
00:42:03,584 --> 00:42:04,585
Of course I know.

522
00:42:05,344 --> 00:42:08,115
Pad Thai without bean sprouts and a green soda.

523
00:42:15,027 --> 00:42:17,428
Do you really know everything about me?

524
00:42:21,406 --> 00:42:24,446
Just some things. There are things I don't know.

525
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:27,360
You're hard to figure out.

526
00:42:30,900 --> 00:42:31,920
And you're hard to get close to.

527
00:42:36,211 --> 00:42:38,656
Just look at today. You suddenly asked me to meet you.

528
00:42:39,067 --> 00:42:40,840
Even though you never wanted to talk to me before.

529
00:42:41,904 --> 00:42:44,120
And now that I'm here, you keep asking me all these weird questions.

530
00:42:48,480 --> 00:42:50,000
Isn't it a good thing that I asked to see you?

531
00:42:54,350 --> 00:42:55,351
It is, but...

532
00:42:57,539 --> 00:42:58,760
It just feels out of character for you.

533
00:43:01,144 --> 00:43:02,880
Just tell me what you really want.

534
00:43:07,245 --> 00:43:09,760
Stop chasing after me. You're annoying.

535
00:43:13,395 --> 00:43:15,614
You're handsome, but you look like an alpaca.

536
00:43:15,848 --> 00:43:17,256
And you're so old-fashioned and awkward.

537
00:43:17,598 --> 00:43:18,920
I don't want a boyfriend like that.

538
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:24,240
My boyfriend is a thousand times better than you.

539
00:43:24,376 --> 00:43:26,264
Why would I want you following me around

540
00:43:26,328 --> 00:43:28,300
and sucking up to me like a clingy little pest?

541
00:43:28,536 --> 00:43:30,880
And stop taking pictures and tagging me in them!

542
00:43:31,107 --> 00:43:34,280
I don't want people knowing some alpaca is chasing after me.
It's embarrassing!

543
00:43:55,526 --> 00:43:56,920
I was just checking if you had a fever.

544
00:44:00,560 --> 00:44:02,120
You must've been holding a lot in, huh?

545
00:44:04,459 --> 00:44:06,078
If yelling at me makes you feel better,

546
00:44:06,528 --> 00:44:08,208
go ahead. I can take it.

547
00:44:09,312 --> 00:44:11,000
As much as you want. Come on.

548
00:44:16,667 --> 00:44:18,520
What? You're not going to yell at me anymore?

549
00:44:22,547 --> 00:44:25,304
Hey, that guy who's been pursuing Ta...

550
00:44:25,987 --> 00:44:27,088
I put him to the test.

551
00:44:28,051 --> 00:44:29,326
No matter how much I insulted him, he didn't get angry.

552
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:32,192
He even worried that I might have a fever.

553
00:44:33,239 --> 00:44:34,240
What do you think?

554
00:44:35,093 --> 00:44:37,560
Can we rule him out as a murder suspect now?

555
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:49,812
Auntie.

556
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:53,000
Do you think the director and Mutta have broken things off yet?

557
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:56,840
How would I know? I wasn't hiding under their bed!

558
00:44:56,910 --> 00:44:57,911
I have no idea.

559
00:44:58,480 --> 00:45:00,560
I bet they're not over yet. Wanna bet?

560
00:45:02,054 --> 00:45:04,840
Count me in. I'll bet a thousand baht.

561
00:45:07,878 --> 00:45:09,560
This is a government office.

562
00:45:09,910 --> 00:45:11,480
You can't go around gambling here.

563
00:45:12,827 --> 00:45:13,828
How much are you betting?

564
00:45:14,086 --> 00:45:15,087
Two thousand baht.

565
00:45:20,294 --> 00:45:23,560
- Hello, Director.
- Hello, hello.

566
00:45:25,523 --> 00:45:26,524
Your coffee, sir.

567
00:45:27,096 --> 00:45:28,097
All right, let's begin.

568
00:45:29,848 --> 00:45:31,760
Here's the schedule for the fundraising event.

569
00:45:32,483 --> 00:45:34,152
Starting at 5 p.m.,

570
00:45:34,628 --> 00:45:36,787
the staff will arrive at the hotel to set up.

571
00:45:37,491 --> 00:45:40,140
At 6 p.m., guests will start arriving.

572
00:45:40,262 --> 00:45:41,263
Oh!

573
00:45:42,016 --> 00:45:43,160
You're back at work already?

574
00:45:46,230 --> 00:45:47,560
Yes, Director.

575
00:45:55,725 --> 00:45:58,024
At 7 p.m., you'll give the opening speech, sir.

576
00:45:58,056 --> 00:46:00,560
- Send the schedule to Veekit.
- Yes, sir.

577
00:46:00,763 --> 00:46:03,088
As for you, come see me in my office.

578
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:26,000
See? I told you they weren't over.

579
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:28,240
Of course I believe you! I believed it before you did.

580
00:46:28,358 --> 00:46:29,360
What's going on?

581
00:46:39,694 --> 00:46:41,200
Oh, the VIP guests.

582
00:46:48,022 --> 00:46:50,320
- How many tables are we setting up?
- Let me write that down.

583
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:00,241
Ta.

584
00:47:01,062 --> 00:47:02,600
It's your first day back at work,

585
00:47:03,174 --> 00:47:05,248
and the director's already summoned you to his office?

586
00:47:05,771 --> 00:47:07,050
How lucky!

587
00:47:10,662 --> 00:47:12,240
Isn't that great, Chom?

588
00:47:12,700 --> 00:47:13,701
Absolutely!

589
00:47:15,560 --> 00:47:17,280
Everyone! Everyone!

590
00:47:17,500 --> 00:47:18,501
Hey, everyone!

591
00:47:19,515 --> 00:47:24,032
Chom, you shouldn't talk about something so embarrassing.

592
00:47:26,453 --> 00:47:29,640
Don't worry, Ta. I'm rooting for you.

593
00:47:42,558 --> 00:47:44,200
I'm raising my bet by 500 baht.

594
00:47:44,392 --> 00:47:46,040
- I'm raising mine too.
- Now, listen.

595
00:47:46,123 --> 00:47:48,560
- If we were really betting, how much would you put in?
- We can't! It's illegal!

596
00:48:23,224 --> 00:48:24,225
Ta.

597
00:48:28,254 --> 00:48:29,255
Come in.

598
00:48:38,414 --> 00:48:40,080
Hey, Veekit.

599
00:48:42,568 --> 00:48:44,755
Is he going to scold me for missing work?

600
00:48:46,334 --> 00:48:48,440
What should I say so I don't get fired?

601
00:48:50,539 --> 00:48:52,192
You know he would never fire you.

602
00:48:57,712 --> 00:48:58,760
Ta, can I ask you a favor?

603
00:48:59,430 --> 00:49:00,760
Please don't let anything like that happen again.

604
00:49:02,123 --> 00:49:03,124
Anything like that?

605
00:49:04,584 --> 00:49:05,585
What do you mean?

606
00:49:10,280 --> 00:49:11,760
So you're still not going to end it, are you?

607
00:49:14,374 --> 00:49:15,375
Fine. Do whatever you want.

608
00:50:07,576 --> 00:50:08,840
I'm sorry, Director.

609
00:50:09,438 --> 00:50:12,160
From now on, I'll always submit a leave request.

610
00:50:12,170 --> 00:50:13,955
And I won't disappear for so long again.

611
00:50:15,070 --> 00:50:18,000
- I promise I'll catch up on all my work...
- I've moved on, Ta.

612
00:50:20,536 --> 00:50:21,537
What did you say?

613
00:50:23,688 --> 00:50:25,288
When you first disappeared,

614
00:50:25,758 --> 00:50:27,050
I was practically losing my mind.

615
00:50:32,269 --> 00:50:33,720
But as time went by,

616
00:50:35,698 --> 00:50:36,960
I started to come to terms with the fact

617
00:50:39,506 --> 00:50:40,600
that you'd left me.

618
00:50:42,296 --> 00:50:43,480
I've moved on, Ta.

619
00:50:49,443 --> 00:50:50,600
But I'm back now, aren't I?

620
00:50:58,267 --> 00:50:59,268
Ta.

621
00:51:01,880 --> 00:51:03,040
Please don't disappear on me again.

622
00:51:03,933 --> 00:51:04,934
Promise me.

623
00:51:06,384 --> 00:51:07,385
I promise.

624
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:09,920
I won't go anywhere again.

625
00:51:17,331 --> 00:51:18,332
That's my girl.

626
00:51:19,667 --> 00:51:21,300
And how's the baby?

627
00:51:22,168 --> 00:51:23,169
The baby?

628
00:51:24,752 --> 00:51:25,753
Yes.

629
00:51:26,891 --> 00:51:27,892
Our baby.

630
00:52:04,435 --> 00:52:05,436
Ta?

631
00:52:05,608 --> 00:52:07,096
Ta, what's wrong?

632
00:52:10,910 --> 00:52:11,911
Come sit down.

633
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:14,401
What's the matter, Ta?

634
00:52:14,779 --> 00:52:15,780
I had a miscarriage.

635
00:52:16,491 --> 00:52:17,492
I lost the baby.

636
00:52:17,771 --> 00:52:18,772
What?

637
00:52:20,843 --> 00:52:21,844
A miscarriage?

638
00:52:25,192 --> 00:52:26,193
But...

639
00:52:27,022 --> 00:52:30,620
How did it happen? Why did you miscarry? Tell me.

640
00:52:33,771 --> 00:52:34,772
It was an accident.

641
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:40,921
Ta.

642
00:52:42,640 --> 00:52:44,320
Ta, it's okay.

643
00:52:46,582 --> 00:52:47,840
You did everything you could.

644
00:52:49,451 --> 00:52:50,840
It wasn't your fault.

645
00:52:52,400 --> 00:52:53,440
Don't blame yourself.

646
00:52:56,768 --> 00:52:57,769
From now on,

647
00:52:59,067 --> 00:53:00,440
I won't let this happen again.

648
00:53:02,320 --> 00:53:03,321
And as for you,

649
00:53:04,678 --> 00:53:07,520
get a contraceptive implant so you won't get pregnant again.

650
00:53:09,219 --> 00:53:10,220
What did you say?

651
00:53:11,603 --> 00:53:12,920
You want me to get a contraceptive implant?

652
00:53:14,718 --> 00:53:17,040
Yes. We already talked about this.

653
00:53:17,835 --> 00:53:19,520
We can't risk another pregnancy.

654
00:53:23,392 --> 00:53:24,393
Okay.

655
00:53:27,670 --> 00:53:28,671
Ta.

656
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:31,301
I've missed you so much.

657
00:53:33,622 --> 00:53:35,280
Please don't ever leave me again, Ta.

658
00:53:47,294 --> 00:53:48,295
My sweet Ta.

659
00:53:51,928 --> 00:53:53,240
I've missed you so much.

660
00:53:55,478 --> 00:53:56,479
Ta!

661
00:53:57,464 --> 00:54:00,120
Hong, please. Just tell me what happened.

662
00:54:00,456 --> 00:54:01,720
Who pushed me down the stairs?

663
00:54:04,478 --> 00:54:06,520
Why do you want me to tell you, Ta?

664
00:54:07,203 --> 00:54:09,040
You were the one it happened to.

665
00:54:10,440 --> 00:54:12,320
I was a little disoriented at the time.

666
00:54:12,547 --> 00:54:15,440
I hit my head when I fell, so I lost my memory.

667
00:54:16,040 --> 00:54:18,840
Please tell me, Hong. There's no one else here. You can tell me.

668
00:54:31,048 --> 00:54:32,520
I have to be careful.

669
00:54:32,835 --> 00:54:34,840
I'm afraid I'll get fired.

670
00:54:37,030 --> 00:54:38,560
Here's what happened.

671
00:54:38,870 --> 00:54:39,871
Mutta, you bitch!

672
00:54:40,560 --> 00:54:41,561
Stop right there!

673
00:54:43,408 --> 00:54:44,409
Mutta, you bitch!

674
00:54:45,243 --> 00:54:46,500
I said stop right now!

675
00:54:46,840 --> 00:54:47,841
Stop!

676
00:54:56,606 --> 00:54:57,920
Where did you get that ring?

677
00:55:05,512 --> 00:55:06,760
Someone gave it to me.

678
00:55:14,147 --> 00:55:16,880
Jenphop proposed to me with that ring.

679
00:55:18,760 --> 00:55:22,280
He had it custom-made just for me.

680
00:55:24,824 --> 00:55:26,180
How could you possibly have the same ring?

681
00:55:33,686 --> 00:55:34,840
Well, maybe that means

682
00:55:37,790 --> 00:55:39,491
you're not the only special one in his life.

683
00:55:51,219 --> 00:55:52,760
How dare you! Huh?

684
00:55:53,875 --> 00:55:54,920
Please don't make a scene, ma'am.

685
00:55:55,304 --> 00:55:56,792
Director Jenphop is heading this way, too.

686
00:55:58,438 --> 00:56:01,240
Go and stop Jenphop! I'll deal with this bitch!

687
00:56:01,808 --> 00:56:02,809
Ma'am!

688
00:56:02,838 --> 00:56:05,120
I said go! Now!

689
00:56:06,091 --> 00:56:07,092
Yes, ma'am.

690
00:56:12,470 --> 00:56:13,760
No one's coming to help you now.

691
00:56:15,300 --> 00:56:17,040
It's just you and me.

692
00:56:18,496 --> 00:56:21,160
Director, I have some documents for you to look at.

693
00:56:22,798 --> 00:56:23,799
What documents?

694
00:56:24,453 --> 00:56:25,454
Just a moment. Let me find them.

695
00:56:28,067 --> 00:56:30,160
Quick! Record this historic moment!

696
00:56:30,286 --> 00:56:32,382
Why the hell don't you film it yourself?

697
00:56:32,400 --> 00:56:33,720
My phone's out of storage!

698
00:56:36,259 --> 00:56:37,260
Ma'am.

699
00:56:38,260 --> 00:56:40,720
Quite a crowd is gathering, ma'am.

700
00:56:46,000 --> 00:56:47,760
Take pictures of everyone here!

701
00:56:49,645 --> 00:56:51,160
If word of this ever gets out,

702
00:56:51,584 --> 00:56:52,760
I'll make every last one of you pay!

703
00:56:54,051 --> 00:56:55,052
Yes, ma'am.

704
00:57:01,798 --> 00:57:02,799
All done, ma'am.

705
00:57:11,160 --> 00:57:12,161
All this time,

706
00:57:13,400 --> 00:57:15,160
you've been sneaking around in secret.

707
00:57:17,142 --> 00:57:19,800
Today, I'll make sure everyone knows who you are!

708
00:57:21,406 --> 00:57:22,407
Come here!

709
00:57:27,827 --> 00:57:28,828
Everyone!

710
00:57:29,560 --> 00:57:30,880
Take a good look at this bitch!

711
00:57:32,094 --> 00:57:34,360
She looks innocent, but she's a shameless slut!

712
00:57:34,522 --> 00:57:35,840
She's been sleeping with another woman's husband!

713
00:57:38,483 --> 00:57:40,400
If you ever see her again,

714
00:57:40,763 --> 00:57:43,880
you have my permission to spit in her face!

715
00:57:50,235 --> 00:57:53,280
Everyone, if you're going to spit at her,

716
00:57:53,510 --> 00:57:54,800
make sure you aim carefully.

717
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:57,301
Because if you miss and your spit lands on the ground,

718
00:57:57,531 --> 00:57:59,760
you could be fined for littering!

719
00:58:00,403 --> 00:58:01,404
Come here!

720
00:58:02,531 --> 00:58:05,100
Where's everyone running? Is something happening outside?

721
00:58:06,483 --> 00:58:07,920
Maybe they're going to buy lottery tickets.

722
00:58:12,440 --> 00:58:13,960
It's time for a mistress like you

723
00:58:15,038 --> 00:58:18,500
to learn what happens when you steal a wife’s husband!

724
00:58:33,130 --> 00:58:36,080
Nopnapha sure knows how to deliver a slap!

725
00:58:36,131 --> 00:58:38,300
Look at that! She's getting slapped so fast I can't even count!

726
00:58:38,350 --> 00:58:39,351
Exactly, Auntie.

727
00:58:40,147 --> 00:58:41,648
I feel so sorry for her.

728
00:58:42,518 --> 00:58:43,960
If I could take some of those slaps for her,

729
00:58:44,384 --> 00:58:46,840
I'd gladly share her pain.

730
00:58:47,616 --> 00:58:50,320
Oh, Hong, dear.

731
00:58:50,702 --> 00:58:52,146
Don't just stand there talking.

732
00:58:52,574 --> 00:58:54,050
Go on up there, then.

733
00:58:58,883 --> 00:59:00,360
You thought I was too high and mighty

734
00:59:01,123 --> 00:59:03,440
to stoop to dealing with someone like you, didn't you?

735
00:59:05,107 --> 00:59:06,120
Well, now you know

736
00:59:06,936 --> 00:59:07,937
how wrong you were!

737
00:59:10,579 --> 00:59:11,820
When it comes to mistresses,

738
00:59:12,580 --> 00:59:14,481
there's no level I won't stoop to!

739
00:59:19,462 --> 00:59:21,320
Huh? What did you say?

740
00:59:22,526 --> 00:59:23,640
Didn't hear me clearly?

741
00:59:25,160 --> 00:59:26,620
Let me clean out your ears for you!

742
00:59:28,856 --> 00:59:30,600
Just send them to me when you find them.

743
00:59:30,718 --> 00:59:32,480
Found them, sir! Here they are!

744
00:59:56,075 --> 00:59:57,076
Ta!

745
01:00:00,816 --> 01:00:02,160
- Is she dead?
- Hurry! Help her!

746
01:00:02,680 --> 01:00:04,520
- Ta!
- She's not moving!

747
01:00:04,606 --> 01:00:05,607
Ta!

748
01:00:08,094 --> 01:00:09,095
Ta, are you okay?

749
01:00:11,726 --> 01:00:14,120
Nopnapha, have you lost your mind?

750
01:00:14,376 --> 01:00:15,760
Are you trying to kill her?

751
01:00:17,078 --> 01:00:19,520
If I wanted to kill her, she'd be dead by now!

752
01:00:22,933 --> 01:00:24,440
I'm not letting her die that easily!

753
01:00:25,147 --> 01:00:26,248
That would be too easy for her!

754
01:00:26,928 --> 01:00:29,080
If you don't stay away from my husband,

755
01:00:29,974 --> 01:00:31,300
I'll make sure you suffer again!

756
01:00:37,736 --> 01:00:39,080
It's a miracle, isn't it?

757
01:00:39,320 --> 01:00:41,760
She fell down the stairs but survived.

758
01:00:42,195 --> 01:00:43,196
That's true.

759
01:00:51,539 --> 01:00:52,540
Ta.

760
01:00:54,424 --> 01:00:55,425
Ta!

761
01:00:57,854 --> 01:00:59,478
Are you really that shocked?

762
01:01:00,536 --> 01:01:02,700
That's exactly what happened that day.

763
01:01:02,800 --> 01:01:04,840
I didn't exaggerate or make anything up.

764
01:01:31,600 --> 01:01:33,881
You really do look much more radiant, Nopnapha.

765
01:01:34,014 --> 01:01:37,640
I simply got rid of something that had been bothering me.

766
01:01:39,480 --> 01:01:40,500
Every problem

767
01:01:41,000 --> 01:01:44,601
must be dealt with directly and decisively.
Only then can we have peace of mind.

768
01:01:45,112 --> 01:01:46,280
You hurt my sister!

769
01:01:46,678 --> 01:01:49,000
I won't let a cruel, heartless monster like you

770
01:01:49,603 --> 01:01:51,960
continue to walk around in society as if nothing happened.

771
01:01:52,851 --> 01:01:53,920
You bitch, Nopnapha!

772
01:02:05,366 --> 01:02:08,480
We haven't done it in two weeks. I've really missed your moves, Director.

773
01:02:08,656 --> 01:02:10,160
I didn't know you could talk so dirty.

774
01:02:14,707 --> 01:02:16,408
If you don't want Aunt Nopnapha to hurt you,

775
01:02:16,654 --> 01:02:18,200
just stay away from Uncle Jenphop.

776
01:02:18,451 --> 01:02:20,000
The old Mutta is gone.

777
01:02:28,126 --> 01:02:30,400
I can't wait to see them get into a catfight at the event!
